hypotheses.statement:
Each $h_N:M\to U$ is a continuously differentiable bijection with continuously differentiable inverse, and $$\label{eq:hN-bounds}
 (1-4c)\|x-x'\|\le\|h_N(x)-h_N(x')\|
             \le(1+4c)\|x-x'\|.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
$L_\xi:M\to U$ is an onto linear isometry. If $y=(y_n)\in U$ and $\beta_n=\langle\xi_n,y_n\rangle$, its inverse is $$\label{eq:frozen-inverse}
 (L_\xi^{-1}y)_{U_m}
 =y_m-\beta_m\xi_m+\beta_{2m}\xi_m,\qquad
 (L_\xi^{-1}y)_{V_m}=\beta_{2m-1}.$$

Each $h_N:M\to U$ is a continuously differentiable bijection with continuously differentiable inverse, and $$\label{eq:hN-bounds}
 (1-4c)\|x-x'\|\le\|h_N(x)-h_N(x')\|
             \le(1+4c)\|x-x'\|.$$
